  "enhanced_information": "The 13-year-old girl's symptoms and CSF findings of lymphocytic predominance and normal glucose levels suggest viral meningitis, likely caused by Echovirus, particularly given her recent exposure at a summer camp. This diagnosis is supported by evidence linking lymphocytes predominantly with viral infections and specifically with Echoviruses.",
